{"Falsy check 'if client_sample_rate:' evaluates to False when client_sample_rate is 0.0, which is a valid sample rate value, causing events with 0% sample rate to not have sample_rate set on normalized_data": 0.7042874693870544, "hash() produces different cache keys across worker processes because Python's hash() is randomized per process via PYTHONHASHSEED, causing cache.set() in one worker to never be found by cache.get() in another worker in multi-worker deployments": 0.9607930183410645, "upsampled_count function references sample_weight column that doesn't appear in the codebase's schema definitions, column mappings, or event processing pipeline - queries using upsampled_count will fail at runtime if this column doesn't exist": 0.6866932511329651, "toInt64 used instead of toUInt64 - inconsistent with all other count aggregations in the file which use toUInt64 (5 occurrences at lines 1194, 1218, 1355, 1368, 1370)": 0.39790987968444824, "default_result_type=\"number\" differs from the regular count function's \"integer\" type, which may affect downstream result parsing": 0.5436134338378906, "Substring match '\"event.type:error\" in query' can produce false positives, matching queries like 'event.type:error_something' or 'not event.type:error', incorrectly enabling upsampling for non-error queries": 0.9406704306602478, "organization parameter declared but never used in _are_all_projects_error_upsampled(project_ids, organization) function": 0.15051902830600739}